.TH cargo-cleanme 1 0.2.5 https://github.com/dbowm91/cargo-cleanme "General Commands Manual"
.SH NAME
cargo\-cleanme \- Clean inactive Cargo build artifacts through Cargo, or reconcile the machine read\-only
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBcargo\-cleanme\fR [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-progress\fR] [\fB\-\-stats\fR] [\fB\-\-format\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Clean inactive Cargo build artifacts through Cargo, or reconcile the machine read\-only
.PP
INVOCATION
             After installation the binary is invoked by Cargo as an external
             subcommand, so the supported spelling is:
.PP
             	cargo cleanme [SUBCOMMAND] [OPTIONS]
.PP
             A directly downloaded binary is invoked as
	cargo\-cleanme [SUBCOMMAND] [OPTIONS]
.PP
             Both spellings accept exactly the same arguments.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<CONFIG>\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-no\-progress\fR
Disable transient progress UI (useful for benchmarks and debugging)
.TP
\fB\-\-stats\fR
Print detailed scan/cleanup counters and phase timings to stderr. Never changes deterministic stdout. `\-\-no\-progress \-\-stats` is the canonical benchmark/debug combination
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<FORMAT>\fR [default: human]
Select human\-readable output, the versioned JSON automation contract, or one bounded ASCII summary line for unattended schedulers
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
human
.IP \(bu 2
json
.IP \(bu 2
log: One bounded ASCII summary line per report, for unattended schedulers that retain a short history tail. Not a machine contract: complete consumers use `json`
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Simulate: run every decision, proof, and reporting step, but invoke no `cargo clean` process at all. Honoured wherever it appears, so the `cargo cleanme \-\-dry\-run clean ROOT` spelling cannot fall back to Execute
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
cargo\-cleanme\-scan(1)
Reconcile the machine read\-only: full by default, explicit with ROOT, routine inventory with `\-\-known`
.TP
cargo\-cleanme\-config(1)
.TP
cargo\-cleanme\-clean(1)
Preview or execute cleanup of revalidated Cargo build artifacts
.TP
cargo\-cleanme\-update(1)
Update this cargo\-cleanme to the latest stable published release
.SH VERSION
v0.2.5
